error[E0277]: this subscriber has no batches to size
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_slots_without_a_slice_body.rs:20:26
   |
20 |     let _capped = handle.batch(nonzero!(64));
   |                          ^^^^^ `batch(..)` sizes the batches a batch body is handed
   |
help: the trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsBatches` is not implemented for `handle`
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_slots_without_a_slice_body.rs:13:1
   |
13 | #[subscriber("orders")]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: the batch size belongs to a batch body (`&[T]`, `&[F<'_>]`, `&[Message<H, P>]`), with or without a reply and `Out` slots; a single-message body takes no batch, and how many of those are in flight at once is `workers(n)` instead
   = help: the following other types implement trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsBatches`:
             HandleValue<BatchDeserialized<F>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<BatchPair<Hd, P>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<ruststream::runtime::Batch<T>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             ReplyValue<V, Dest>
             Sealed<V>
   = note: required for `SubscriberBuilder<handle, Name, (Open, Open, Open, Open)>` to implement `BatchStep`
   = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `subscriber` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
